://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103768#issuecomment-3511698116","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103768","id":3511698116,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RUELE","user":{"login":"HolonProduction","id":99511741,"node_id":"U_kgDOBe5tvQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/99511741?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction","html_url":"https://github.com/HolonProduction","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/HolonProduction/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-10T13:34:42Z","updated_at":"2025-11-10T13:34:42Z","body":"Could you double check whether you included unrelated changes? The diff contains some create dialog changes in editor interface, for which it's not directly obvious to me how they relate to this PR.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3511698116/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3512183442","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103768#issuecomment-3512183442","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103768","id":3512183442,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RV6qS","user":{"login":"produno","id":8760003,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NjAwMDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8760003?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno","html_url":"https://github.com/produno","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-10T14:50:31Z","updated_at":"2025-11-10T14:51:22Z","body":"> Yeah, I understand your point, but as I said this **does not break compatibility as possible** and **you can configure it and turn it off**. So you can keep the current codestyle you've been using.\r\n\r\nThis wasn't really the point I was trying to make. I **do** want a way to mark my variables as private or public, so I will use whatever is ultimately implemented. But imo having proper access modifiers is the correct way to go, for reasons previously mentioned. So if this is going to hinder or even halt that feature being merged in the future, then that is not good. Hence my question. It also helps me decide if I should use this feature at all if it ends up being merged, as I don't want to break all saves in the future when needing to change.\r\n\r\nFor some of us working on large projects, whom plan to release into Early access, its helpful to give us an idea of what's planned or likely to change/happen regarding certain features, so we can then make informed decisions within our own codebase.\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3512183442/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3512495466","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103768#issuecomment-3512495466","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103768","id":3512495466,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RXG1q","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-10T15:43:41Z","updated_at":"2025-11-10T15:50:44Z","body":"> > Yeah, I understand your point, but as I said this **does not break compatibility as possible** and **you can configure it and turn it off**. So you can keep the current codestyle you've been using.\r\n> \r\n> This wasn't really the point I was trying to make. I **do** want a way to mark my variables as private or public, so I will use whatever is ultimately implemented. But imo having proper access modifiers is the correct way to go, for reasons previously mentioned. So if this is going to hinder or even halt that feature being merged in the future, then that is not good. \r\n\r\nThe feature **won't** eliminate the solution to introduce either a keyword `private` or a modifying annotation `@private`, and you can easily upgrade your grammar from what it presents in this pr to what you have suggested for the future releases (perhaps) when needed because this doesn't take too much time to do grammar migration.\r\n\r\n> Hence my question. It also helps me decide if I should use this feature at all if it ends up being merged, as I don't want to break all saves in the future when needing to change.\r\n\r\nThis is implemented by warnings, so you can disable them in your project settings or enable them as you wish. The warnings will not break your current project *as long as you do not switch the warnings to errors*.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3512495466/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3512572893","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103768#issuecomment-3512572893","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103768","id":3512572893,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RXZvd","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-10T15:58:47Z","updated_at":"2025-11-10T16:07:14Z","body":"@produno Can you explain which feature you're using that changing variable names breaks compatibility? I assume you're passing some of your objects directly into one of the serialization functions, without specifying key names explicitly?\r\n\r\n> For some of us working on large projects, whom plan to release into Early access, its helpful to give us an idea of what's planned or likely to change/happen regarding certain features, so we can then make informed decisions within our own codebase.\r\n\r\nWhile there was a consensus in a previous GDScript meeting that this PR was desirable, it is still up for debate. If we find it is not mergeable due to other concerns, it will not be merged.\r\nIf you'd like to stay up to date with plans, the best place to find out is the dev releases' blogposts on the website. Changes are always up for debate until the moment they're merged (and rarely, they are reverted even after that).\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3512572893/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3512674270","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103768#issuecomment-3512674270","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103768","id":3512674270,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7RXyfe","user":{"login":"produno","id":8760003,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NjAwMDM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8760003?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno","html_url":"https://github.com/produno","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/produno/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-10T16:23:35Z","updated_at":"2025-11-10T16:23:35Z","body":"> @produno Can you explain which feature you're using that changing variable names breaks compatibility? I assume you're passing some of your objects directly into one of the serialization functions, without specifying key names explicitly?\r\n\r\nI save the property name with its value, then upon load I use `set()` to restore the value where required. I'm sure I am not only person serialising in this way. It just means if this is added and proper access modifiers will likely to be added in the future, then I will refrain from using this feature.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3512674270/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3541403644","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103768#issuecomment-3541403644","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103768","id":3541403644,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7TFYf8","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-17T11:51:10Z","updated_at":"2025-11-17T11:51:10Z","body":"Currently there is either using `@private` instead of `_`, or implementing the access restriction for GDScript (which would require the core team for a meeting to decide on this), and also keeping introducing `_` first.\r\n\r\n- For the `@private`, the code will be easily ported, but users are required to type more letters than a single `_`. Meanwhile, based on the conflict raised by `abstract` being `@abstract`, I don't hope to see the same dramma or disaster happen again.\r\n- For the access restriction for GDScript (forced errors and runtime checks), this may require a core team for a meeting on this topic because some details may involve the core part of the engine. Also, it's still a problem to run runtime check with the least cost on performance, so I think this would be far a long time to do.\r\n- For the original idea - using `_`, even though it solves the problem of not having access restriction in GDScript, the naming will also shadows the naming convention of virtual methods that would be public to call (although in most of time they are not called from external places). Meanwhile, it only pops warning if they don't follow the convention, and the game will not stop running after being exported with the release template. However, this is the most convenient and the most balanced (currently) solution to the problem. Of course, it's also a temporary solution, so in the future one of the previous two would replace this.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3541403644/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3616634726","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103768#issuecomment-3616634726","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103768","id":3616634726,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XkXdm","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T12:10:39Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T12:10:52Z","body":"pushed an update thatt is unrelated to this pr (exactly saying, it's about the create_dialog.cpp, but I'd no idea why the update conflicted with this one...)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3616634726/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4760712919","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103768#issuecomment-4760712919","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103768","id":4760712919,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABG8K21w","user":{"login":"Lazy-Rabbit-2001","id":22123964,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMTIzOTY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22123964?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","html_url":"https://github.com/Lazy-Rabbit-2001","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Lazy-Rabbit-2001/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://